Observations (not FAIL)
=====================================================================
O1. Oracle-clause precision (lead artifact, for the record). In
    .swarm/tier3/RC3/rc3_oracle_test.go:301 the ended-row check bans
    `id="expense-end-month-exp-ended"` and `expense-start-month-exp-ended"`.
    No template ever renders that id shape — the real pattern is
    `expense-start-{{.ID}}` i.e. `expense-start-exp-ended`
    (`grep -rn 'expense-start-month-\|expense-end-month-' web/templates/`
    returns nothing). Those two clauses are therefore vacuous; the oracle's
    real teeth on that line are the `hx-put="/whatif/expense/exp-ended"` clause
    (which did fire under MUT A). The SHIPPED test uses the CORRECT ids
    (`id="expense-start-exp-ended"`, `id="expense-end-exp-ended"`,
    `id="expense-schedule-exp-ended"`) and caught MUT A on all three, so the
    behaviour is genuinely guarded and criterion 3 is met. Worth fixing in the
    oracle only if the directory is reused.
O2. One-sided regression guard on the ended-row branch. The income and expense
    templates carry twin `{{if scheduleEnded .EndMonth}}` blocks, but only the
    EXPENSE branch has a shipped test
    (TestRenderExpenseSourcesList_EndedRowIsDisplayOnly; the handler-level
    clamped test also uses an expense, exp-ended). I rendered the income branch
    myself and it is correct (evidence under criterion 3), but deleting just
    the income `{{if scheduleEnded}}` would not fail any shipped test — MUT A
    was caught through the expense branch. V3-pattern promote candidate: an
    income twin of the render test. Not a criterion-6 failure (criterion 6 asks
    for template render tests, and one exists for this behaviour).
O3. Pre-existing dual formatters of a scheduled month, untouched by RC3 and
    outside its manifests: internal/handlers/whatif/verdict.go:94,102
    (`Format("Jan 2006")`) and handlers_spending_optimizer.go:746-750 /
    analysis/spending_funding.go:196 (`Format("2006-01")`). The last of these is
    already in SPEC.md §5 backlog from RC3/checker-second; verdict.go and the
    optimizer handler are not. Backlog only.
O4. web/templates/components/whatif/guardrails.html:122 still renders
    "Year {{.Year}}:". It is a guardrail-ladder table, not one of the four
    schedule surfaces criterion 3 enumerates, and it is byte-identical to
